# HAL car context — copy to ~/.config/hal-context.yaml on the Pi and fill in.
# Injected into Claude's system prompt so HAL knows whose car it's in. Optional:
# a missing file just means HAL is a little less personal. Not a secret, but it
# lives in ~/.config (off the repo) alongside hal.env.
#
#   cp scripts/hal-context.yaml.example ~/.config/hal-context.yaml
#   $EDITOR ~/.config/hal-context.yaml
#
# Maintenance history CSV lives in data/ (repo) and is referenced below.
# setup.sh leaves an existing ~/.config/hal-context.yaml untouched.

car: 1989 BMW 325i Sedan in Delphi Grey Metallic with tan interior
owner: Dave
home_city: El Sobrante

vins:
  chassis: WBAAD1307K8835704
  engine: WBSCD9325WEE7712

summary: |
  Rust-free 1989 BMW 325i 5-speed sedan, daily driver (~300 mi/month for years).
  S52 bottom end with M50 non-Vanos head swap — responsive, punchy, reliable.
  California BAR certified engine swap (sticker on passenger door post); passed
  CA smog three times. Clean title. Chassis ~287k miles; ~20k on drivetrain
  rebuild; ~35k on suspension/bushings/struts.

identity:
  year: 1989
  body: 325i Sedan
  transmission: 5-speed Getrag 260 manual (rebuilt by Zimmerman Automotive, PA)
  exterior: Delphi Grey Metallic (Delphin Grey respray 2012)
  interior: Natur Beige vinyl / tan
  title: clean
  bar_certified: true
  registration_note: CA BAR certified; DMV registered through April 2025
  chassis_miles: ~287000
  drivetrain_miles: 20000
  suspension_miles: 35000

engine_swap:
  - S52 3.2L bottom end / M50 non-Vanos head (raw powerband, E30 character)
  - iX brake booster with relocated reservoir
  - E36 mount arms; E28 M5 motor mounts
  - Offset transmission mount for Getrag 260
  - Fully converted AC (needs inspection/recharge to restore)
  - Zionsville 24v swap AC lines; E36 compressor
  - M3 engine harness covers
  - 413 ECU with Miller chip; also has custom SSSquid tune
  - Zionsville e-fan kit (fan on continuously)
  - New Behr radiator — runs cool
  - Vibrant StreetPower muffler
  - Harness repinned OEM-like (cruise control deleted; oil level sensor/light deleted — no false CELs)

motor:
  - S52 bottom end rebuilt; M50 NV head rebuilt (~20k mi since 2015 rebuild, pre-owner)
  - Machining by Power Performance, San Luis Obispo CA
  - Tolerances verified; cylinders and ring gaps checked
  - Head refreshed with original valves/springs; new valve seats; ARP head studs
  - Chain elongation verified in spec; pulls strong, idles well
  - New late-model coolant reservoir/sensor
  - S52 pink-top injectors (21.5 lb/hr)

transmission_drivetrain:
  - Rebuilt Getrag 260 with E30 M3 clutch (Zimmerman, ~16k mi) — also noted as '88 M3 clutch
  - Rebuilt driveshaft
  - Short-shift kit and bushings/carrier from Zionsville Auto
  - 3.25 limited-slip differential; quiet, good lockup

suspension_steering:
  - E30 M3 springs; Bilstein Sport struts
  - Z3 2.7-turn steering rack
  - E36 PS pump and hoses
  - E30 M3 offset control arm bushings
  - Most bushings replaced within last few years

wheels_tires:
  - Euroweave 15" wheels
  - Yokohama S Drive 205/55R15 (also Kumho Ecsta ST 255/50-15 per 2024 service)

exterior:
  - 100% rust-free undercarriage
  - Euro bumper trim; iX body kit (hard mounted); Shadowline trim; iS lip
  - Clean OEM front/rear roundels
  - Paint respray 2012 — fading/patina/chips/cracking on hood and trunk; dent in hood
  - Recent low-speed rear hit (~3 mph at stoplight) — bumper strip replaced; two small shallow dents and paint scratches on bumper; no trunk or frame damage

interior:
  - Well-preserved Natur Beige vinyl; remarkably clean
  - Rare six-cassette storage rack in center console
  - Fully functional gauge cluster with accurate odometer
  - Six-button OBC — no LCD bleed
  - Oil gauge deleted (never wired to check panel post-swap)
  - OEM beige floor mats (out of production)
  - New all-leather shift boot; mushroom E30 M3-style shifter

audio:
  - Kenwood head unit with Bluetooth
  - JL Audio dual 10" subwoofer box in trunk with JL amp — clean highs, strong lows

other_notes:
  - New catalytic converter 2019
  - Behr radiator and hoses replaced 2021
  - Mason Engineering strut bar (matte black powder coat); Garagistic cross-brace
  - Manual sunroof works, leak-free
  - Viper keyless entry and alarm installed June 2024

known_issues:
  - Paint is the main cosmetic concern — ready for refresh (hood/trunk worst)
  - AC converted but needs recharge/inspection
  - Rear bumper cosmetic damage from recent low-speed tap

maintenance_csv: data/vehicle-maintenance-history.csv
maintenance_recent_limit: 12
